// The Fight Cave roster's own animations, converted from the OSRS cache by
// tools/models/animconvosrs.py, which carries each seq's priority, loop count and walkmerge
// labels across unchanged.
//
// Six skeletons, one per monster family: 160 Tz-Kih, 162 Tz-Kek, 164 Tok-Xil, 163 Yt-MejKot and
// Yt-HurKot, 161 Ket-Zek, 159 TzTok-Jad. They play on an OSRS base (base_osrs_*), so each one
// belongs only on the mesh imported from the same cache - a 377 model posed with one of these,
// or the reverse, is the folded-inside-out shape posepreview.py draws.
//
// WHICH ONE IS WHICH WAS MEASURED, not guessed from the ids. Each family's 377 set and its OSRS
// set hold the same number of animations, and within a family the frame counts and priorities
// pair them off uniquely: firebat_attack is 10 frames at priority 6 and so is exactly one OSRS
// seq on skeleton 160. tools/fightcavespec.json holds all 34 pairings and the battery re-derives
// them from the two caches every run. TzTok-Jad's three attacks were rendered on his own mesh as
// well, because his ready and walk are both 16 frames and the record had to settle those two.
//
// osrs_seq_2650 is Jad's stand, and it is NOT here: the TzRek-Jad round converted it first and it
// lives in npc/configs/boss_pets.seq. Two blocks of the same name would be a duplicate symbol.

